Article 10
Prevention of acts of violence against women as referred to in article 6 paragraph (2) letter a, the Regional Government shall undertake efforts as follows:
a. conduct counseling and socialization regarding matters relating to violence against women;
b. conduct socialization on women's rights;
c. endeavor to improve education for women;
d. open skills courses for women to support the economic needs of the family;
e. create employment opportunities for women;
f. provide counseling to immediately report to local authorities if violence against women occurs;
g. empower social community organizations and women's organizations to increase women's knowledge and insight;
h. establish Women's Protection Complaint Posts; and
i. form networks in efforts to prevent violence.

