CHAPTER II
RIGHTS OF WOMEN VICTIMS OF VIOLENCE
Article 5 Every woman victim of violence has the right:
a. to have her dignity and worth as a human being respected;
b. to obtain protection from family, community, Regional Government and/or other parties either temporarily or based on the determination of a protection order from the court;
c. to physical, psychological and sexual health recovery in accordance with the suffering experienced by the Woman Victim of Violence;
d. to special handling related to the confidentiality of the Woman Victim of Violence;
e. to assistance by social workers and legal aid at every level of the examination process in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations;
f. to spiritual guidance services; and
g. to make her own decisions.

Part Five
Article 16
(1) SPM in the field of integrated services for women and children victims of violence aims to guarantee that Women Victims of violence receive the minimum services needed.
(2) SPM in the field of integrated services for Women Victims of violence, includes services:
a. handling of complaints/reports of Victims of Violence Against Women;
b. health services for women Victims of violence;
c. social rehabilitation for women Victims of violence;
d. law enforcement and Legal Aid for women Victims of violence;
e. Repatriation and Social Reintegration for women Victims of violence; and
f. in the event that Women Victims of Violence experience trauma or illness that endangers themselves as a result of acts of violence so as to require immediate assistance, the Regional Government is obligated to provide first aid no later than 7 (seven) days after the complaint is filed.
Article 17
(1) SPM as referred to in Article 16 has performance indicators including:
a. coverage of women victims of violence who receive complaint handling by trained officers within integrated Service units;
b. coverage ...

