Article 3 This Regional Regulation aims to:
a. guarantee the fulfillment of women's rights so they can live and participate optimally in accordance with human dignity and worth;
b. prevent all forms of Violence against Women;
c. provide protection and a sense of security for women victims of violence and discrimination;
d. ensure the implementation of policies, programs, and activities for the protection of women by the region in a systematic, comprehensive, continuous, and integrated manner;
e. increase the commitment of the Regional Government in implementing policies, programs and activities for the protection of women; and
f. encourage institutions that handle the duties and functions of women's empowerment in the Regional Government as well as community institutions in the region to improve performance in efforts to protect women.
Article 14 The scope of this Regional Regulation includes:
a. the rights of women victims of violence;
b. the authority of the Regional Government;
c. planning;
d. Implementation ...

Article 10
Prevention of acts of violence against women as referred to in article 6 paragraph (2) letter a, the Regional Government shall undertake efforts as follows:
a. conduct counseling and socialization regarding matters relating to violence against women;
b. conduct socialization on women's rights;
c. endeavor to improve education for women;
d. open skills courses for women to support the economic needs of the family;
e. create employment opportunities for women;
f. provide counseling to immediately report to local authorities if violence against women occurs;
g. empower social community organizations and women's organizations to increase women's knowledge and insight;
h. establish Women's Protection Complaint Posts; and
i. form networks in efforts to prevent violence.

Article 15
(1) The procedures and mechanisms of integrated Services, include:
a. complaint services;
b. Health Rehabilitation;
c. Social Rehabilitation;
d. Repatriation;
e. Social Reintegration, and
f. Legal Aid.
(2) The implementation of integrated services as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be carried out in accordance with SPM.

