CHAPTER II
RIGHTS OF WOMEN VICTIMS OF VIOLENCE
Article 5 Every woman victim of violence has the right:
a. to have her dignity and worth as a human being respected;
b. to obtain protection from family, community, Regional Government and/or other parties either temporarily or based on the determination of a protection order from the court;
c. to physical, psychological and sexual health recovery in accordance with the suffering experienced by the Woman Victim of Violence;
d. to special handling related to the confidentiality of the Woman Victim of Violence;
e. to assistance by social workers and legal aid at every level of the examination process in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations;
f. to spiritual guidance services; and
g. to make her own decisions.

Article 10
Prevention of acts of violence against women as referred to in article 6 paragraph (2) letter a, the Regional Government shall undertake efforts as follows:
a. conduct counseling and socialization regarding matters relating to violence against women;
b. conduct socialization on women's rights;
c. endeavor to improve education for women;
d. open skills courses for women to support the economic needs of the family;
e. create employment opportunities for women;
f. provide counseling to immediately report to local authorities if violence against women occurs;
g. empower social community organizations and women's organizations to increase women's knowledge and insight;
h. establish Women's Protection Complaint Posts; and
i. form networks in efforts to prevent violence.

CHAPTER IX
ROLE OF THE COMMUNITY
Article 25 (1) In implementing the Protection of Women, the community may: a. establish family partners at the kelurahan / village level;
b. establish women's protection units within community organizations;
c. conduct independent socialization of Women's rights;
d. provide first aid to Women Victims of Violence;
e. report to the competent authority if violence against Women occurs in their environment;
f. prevent the occurrence of acts of violence against women;
g. provide information and/or report acts of violence against women to the competent authority; and
